<article class="env-lemma" id="04HZ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04HZ">Lemma <span data-tag="04HZ">59.33.5</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. The small étale site $S_{\acute{e}tale}$ endowed with its structure sheaf $\mathcal{O}_ S$ is a locally ringed site, see Modules on Sites, Definition <a href="/tag/04EU" data-tag="04EU">18.40.4</a>. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows because the stalks $(\mathcal{O}_ S)_{\overline{s}} = \mathcal{O}^{sh}_{S, \overline{s}}$ are local, and because $S_{\acute{e}tale}$ has enough points, see Lemma <a href="/tag/04HX" data-tag="04HX">59.33.1</a>, Theorem <a href="/tag/03PU" data-tag="03PU">59.29.10</a>, and Remarks <a href="/tag/040S" data-tag="040S">59.29.11</a>. See Modules on Sites, Lemmas <a href="/tag/04ET" data-tag="04ET">18.40.2</a> and <a href="/tag/05D8" data-tag="05D8">18.40.3</a> for the fact that this implies the small étale site is locally ringed. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>